  "description": "“See America,” by artist Alexander Dux, is a color silkscreen poster on board dated between 1936 and 1939. The catalog describes it as promoting tourism for the United States Travel Bureau and showing two people in caverns. Part of the Work Projects Administration Poster Collection, it bears a June 28, 1939 date stamp on the reverse.",
